---
import ContentLayout from "../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { PLATFORM_STYLES } from "../../components/embedGrid/platformStyles";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="How to Watch Multiple Live Streams at Once | Stream Mix"
  description="Learn how to watch multiple Twitch, YouTube, and Kick streams at once in a customizable browser grid with video and chat."
  heading="How to watch multiple live streams at once"
>
  <p>
    Stream Mix puts <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.twitch.text}>Twitch</span>,{
      " "
    }
    <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.youtube.text}>YouTube</span>, and{" "}
    <span class={PLATFORM_STYLES.kick.text}>Kick</span> broadcasts in one draggable
    browser workspace. No account or download is required.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Add your streams</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      Paste a URL such as <code>twitch.tv/channel</code>,{" "}
      <code>youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID</code>, or{" "}
      <code>kick.com/channel</code>. Stream Mix detects the platform
      automatically.
    </li>
    <li>
      Choose Stream + Chat, Stream, or Chat and select <strong>Add</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>Repeat for every perspective you want to follow.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    You can also select a platform manually and enter a Twitch or Kick channel
    name, or a YouTube video ID.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Choose what each window shows</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Stream + Chat</strong> keeps video and conversation together.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Stream</strong> gives the full panel to video.</li>
    <li><strong>Chat</strong> shows only the platform’s conversation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Arrange and save the workspace</h2>
  <p>
    Drag windows by their headers and resize them from either lower corner.
    Positions are saved automatically in your browser. Minimize panels to the
    bottom shelf, or enable Compact mode to hide the site and window headers.
  </p>
  <p>
    The share button copies a link containing the streams, display modes, and
    grid positions. Opening it replaces an existing workspace only after
    confirmation.
  </p>

  <h2>Playback and platform help</h2>
  <p>
    Several video players can use significant bandwidth and processing power. If
    playback stutters, lower the quality of secondary streams, switch some
    panels to Chat, or minimize streams you do not need continuously.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-twitch-streams"
        >Watch multiple Twitch streams</a
      >{" "}
      for channel URLs and Twitch embed troubleshooting.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-youtube-streams"
        >Watch multiple YouTube live streams</a
      >{" "}
      for supported URLs and live chat availability.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/guides/watch-multiple-kick-streams"
        >Watch multiple Kick streams</a
      >{" "}
      for channel inputs and Kick player behavior.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The <a href="/faq">FAQ</a> covers saved layouts, privacy, sharing, and common
    playback issues.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/" class="btn btn-primary">Watch multiple streams</a></p>
</ContentLayout>
